    {
      "questionId": "673c02b5187976f6d72f9ef2",
      "answer": "JSX (JavaScript XML) is a syntax extension for JavaScript used in React to describe what the user interface (UI) should look like. It allows you to write HTML-like code directly within JavaScript, making it easier to visualize the structure of the UI components.\n\nJSX is not a requirement for React but is widely used because it makes the code more readable and expressive. Under the hood, JSX is transformed into regular JavaScript using tools like Babel",
      "_id": {
        "$oid": "674d27d9c0bea15f04d245ee"
      }
    },
    {
      "questionId": "673c0260187976f6d72f9ed6",
      "answer": "JSX (JavaScript XML) is a syntax extension for JavaScript used in React to describe what the user interface (UI) should look like. It allows you to write HTML-like code directly within JavaScript, making it easier to visualize the structure of the UI components.\n\nJSX is not a requirement for React but is widely used because it makes the code more readable and expressive. Under the hood, JSX is transformed into regular JavaScript using tools like Babel",
      "_id": {
        "$oid": "674d27d9c0bea15f04d245ef"
      }
    },
    {
      "questionId": "673c02cd187976f6d72f9ef4",
      "answer": "Reconciliation is the process React uses to update the DOM efficiently when the state or props of a component change. Instead of making direct changes to the actual DOM (which is expensive in terms of performance), React employs a Virtual DOM to optimize updates.\n\nVirtual DOM:\n\nReact creates an in-memory representation of the actual DOM (called the Virtual DOM).\nWhen a component's state or props change, React calculates a new Virtual DOM tree.\nIt then compares the new Virtual DOM tree with the previous one (a process called diffing) to determine the minimal set of changes needed to update the actual DOM.\nDOM Updates:\n\nOnly the parts of the DOM that have changed are updated, reducing expensive DOM manipulation operations.\n",
      "_id": {
        "$oid": "674d27d9c0bea15f04d245f0"
      }
    }
  ],
