      }
    },
    {
      "questionId": "673c037a187976f6d72f9f1a",
      "answer": "In Selenium WebDriver, locating web elements using their ID attribute means identifying a specific element on a webpage by its unique \"id\" value, which is assigned to the element in the HTML code; this is considered the most reliable way to locate an element because each ID should be distinct within a page, allowing for precise interaction with that element in your automation tests. ",
      "_id": {
        "$oid": "67573326c907ac1a802718bd"
      }
